  "warnings": [],
  "working_thesis": "Arendt analyzes the fundamental phenomenological and historical distinctions between labor (the cyclical biological activity of the animal laborans tied to necessity and consumption), work (the world-building fabrication of homo faber guided by utility and instrumentality), and action/thought, detailing how the modern age's elevation of labor and consumer society threatens the durability of the human world."
}
